          caption: "For children the workhorse is nasal prongs at 1–2 L/min (0.5–1 in the newborn) titrated to saturations of 90 per cent or above; the non-rebreather at 10–15 L/min is for the collapsed child while help comes, and a simple mask is never run below 5 L/min.",
