          alt: "Dehydration in children — the three IMCI plans. Plan A, no dehydration, treat at home: extra fluids after each loose stool — 50 to 100 mL under two years, 100 to 200 mL for two years and over — continue breastfeeding and feeding, zinc 10 mg daily under six months or 20 mg from six months for 10 to 14 days, and return if blood in the stool, drinking poorly, fever, or not better in three days. Plan B, some dehydration, ORS at the clinic: 75 mL/kg over four hours by cup and spoon, small sips, wait ten minutes if the child vomits then continue slowly, breastfeed between, reassess at four hours and reclassify. Plan C, severe dehydration, intravenous Ringer's lactate 100 mL/kg: under 12 months 30 mL/kg in the first hour then 70 mL/kg over five hours; 12 months and older 30 mL/kg in 30 minutes then 70 mL/kg over two and a half hours; give ORS as soon as the child can drink; reassess every 15 to 30 minutes and repeat the first bolus if the pulse is still weak; if no IV access, ORS by nasogastric tube 20 mL/kg/h for six hours. In severe acute malnutrition, do not use Plan C — use ReSoMal unless in shock.",
